message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "MLV Tools: Interactive Web Applications for Machine Learning Variance Analysis"
abstract: >-
  MLV Tools is a collection of interactive, browser-based web applications
  developed as a companion to the paper "The Impact of Performance Variability
  on Neural Network Evaluation and its Implications for Model Design". The
  tools allow researchers to reproduce and explore the paper's results
  interactively, and apply the same analyses to their own data. It includes:
  (1) Model & Data Inspector, for visualizing training run distributions across
  conditions and datasets; (2) Replication and Comparison, for estimating the
  probability of misranking models due to variance overlap under limited
  training runs; (3) Ablation Tests, for exploring hyperparameter interactions
  and quantifying the error probability of sequential ablation strategies; and
  (4) Standardizing Comparisons, for planning how many training runs are needed
  to reach a target performance percentile with a given confidence level. All
  tools run entirely in the browser with no installation required. Available
  online at https://enheragu.github.io/mlv-tools/
